from mk import mk
mk("uEI2Ytxn7iI","Deconstructing a Textural Soundscape | Creative Sprint #5 Breakdown",
 "random-modulator-soundscape-loop-voice-playhead-pan-random-delay-octave-feedback",
 "Random-modulator soundscape loop: resampled-chord drone with one random modulator on each voice's start position and pan, randomly shortened arp-driven drums, a randomly retimed delay with a +12 st pitch shifter and stepped grain size in its feedback, and a step-scanned vocal sampler",
 "Keep a slow (88 BPM) textural loop alive using random and step modulators rather than new notes. (1) Drone: resample a plucked chord into a sampler, set it up to sustain, and have one random modulator (no smoothing; slight clicks are accepted as character) move both sample start/playhead and pan, so each voice starts somewhere different and sits elsewhere in the stereo field. Run a delay in parallel with a convolution reverb. (2) Drums: half-note mallet/brush hits from an arpeggiator whose step count is randomly shortened (16 down to a minimum of 4 steps), so the loop never repeats the same way. Send it to a delay whose time in beats is randomly modulated with smoothing (about 1–8 beats), with a pitch shifter at +12 semitones inside the feedback and a step modulator on its grain size for metallic, sideways echoes. (3) Vocal: a vocal loop in a sampler driven by an 8-step transposing arp, a 16-step modulator choosing the playhead start each step, a band-pass with a slow LFO on frequency, random pan per note, a distortion macro stepped through 16 values, then delay with reverse blur. Delta vs our shimmer and granular skills: random/step modulation of sampler playheads and delay timing as the generative engine.",
 ["Sampler with modulatable sample start and pan; random and step modulators (Web Audio: AudioBufferSourceNode.start(when, offset) with a random offset per voice, implementation note)","Arpeggiator with modulatable step count","Delay with modulatable time and an insertable pitch shifter in its feedback path","Band-pass filter, distortion, convolution reverb"],
 [("chord_resample","audio","Rendered pluck/piano chord to turn into a drone",True),("vocal_loop","audio","Original/licensed vocal loop",False),("tempo","number","Slow tempo, e.g. 88 BPM",True)],
 [("soundscape_loop","audio","Evolving multi-layer textural loop that never repeats identically")],
 ["Leaving the playhead randomiser unsmoothed causes clicks. The presenter keeps them as character; smooth or crossfade if they're too loud.","Random delay-time modulation needs smoothing to avoid zipper jumps.","The pitch shifter in the feedback re-pitches every repeat (+12 cascades), so filter if it gets shrill.","Ranges quoted (16→4 steps, 1–8 beats, +12 st, 16 steps) are from the transcript; other amounts by ear."],
 [("Resample a plucked chord into a sampler and set it up to sustain as a drone. Add one random modulator and map it to both sample playhead/start and pan.","drone","Each new voice starts at a different point in the sample and lands at a different pan"),
  ("Process the drone through a standard delay in parallel with a convolution reverb.","drone fx","Atmospheric bed"),
  ("Drums at slow tempo: half-note hits from a drum machine with two samples (mallet, brush) driven by an arpeggiator. Add a random modulator that shortens the arp length by up to −12 steps (16 down to 4).","drums","Sparse percussion whose pattern never repeats the same way"),
  ("Send drums to a delay: random modulator with smoothing on delay time in beats (about 1 to 8), a pitch shifter at +12 semitones inside the feedback loop, and a step modulator on the shifter's grain size.","pitch-feedback delay","Metallic, octave-climbing echoes, especially in the sides"),
  ("Add a background drone layer (e.g. a pad preset with longer envelope/filter and chorus) playing the same chords lower, plus an optional texture drone into a big reverb with modulated warp, kept low in the mix.","fill","Fuller low/mid spectrum without overpowering"),
  ("Vocal layer: vocal loop in a sampler fed by an 8-step arp with transposition. Use a 16-step modulator to set a different playhead start per step, a slow LFO on a band-pass frequency, and a random modulator on pan.","vocal","Chopped, moving vocal fragments across the stereo field"),
  ("Vocal FX: distortion preset whose saturation macro is stepped through 16 values, then a delay with reverse blur.","vocal fx","Rhythmically varying grit and smeared echoes")],
 ["Repeated notes on the drone start from audibly different sample positions and pans.","The drum arp pattern length varies between 4 and 16 steps over successive bars.","Delay repeats climb in pitch by octaves inside the feedback.","Each vocal step begins at a different point of the loop."],
 ["generative","random-modulation","sampler","delay","pitch-shift","soundscape","texture","web-audio"],
 note="Loop breakdown; product presets and pack names omitted.")

mk("KVtxIwYpGvQ","Ableton's best kept secret for ambient textures",
 "stereo-unlinked-micro-loop-buffer-binary-random-freeze-reverse-cross-feedback",
 "Glitchy micro-loop buffer for ambient textures: freeze-and-scan buffer with segment length, pitch that cascades through feedback, temporary pitch from sample-rate steps, unlinked L/R (+12 / −12 st with cross feedback) and binary-random LFOs toggling freeze and reverse per side",
 "Recreate boutique 'micro-looper' pedal textures with one buffer-delay device. A delay whose position = delay time, feedback = repeats, and segment = how much of the capture plays, plus reverse and a hold/freeze that captures the buffer so position scans it. Add random start position (plus an LFO), a short range for finer control, pitch shift (an octave or a fifth; it cascades up with every feedback pass, so use the high-cut), sample-rate steps that create temporary pitch drops and crunch, vibrato, and a low/high-cut band-pass. Unlink L and R for independent positions, segments, pitch and LFOs: L +12 st, R −12 st with cross feedback. Then automate with binary (random on/off) LFOs at unequal rates on freeze L/R and on reverse L/R, plus a random LFO stepping the sample-rate/bandwidth, and optionally a hybrid reverb. Lower dry/wet for a background whisper. Delta vs our granular-freeze, reverb-freeze and shimmer skills: per-channel random binary freeze/reverse and octave-split cross feedback.",
 ["Buffer/looper delay with freeze, position, segment, reverse, pitch, sample-rate and filter controls (Web Audio: AudioWorklet ring buffer with per-channel read heads, implementation note)","LFOs with binary-random and random shapes, mapped as remote (not manual) controls","Optional reverb"],
 [("source","audio","Melodic loop, keys or guitar-like part",True)],
 [("glitch_buffer_texture","audio","Stereo, randomly freezing/reversing micro-loop texture")],
 ["Pitch inside feedback cascades with each repeat: an octave (or a fifth) is plenty; two octaves gets shrill. Use the high-cut.","Sample-rate changes momentarily shift pitch (that's the effect); don't smooth them away.","Binary LFO rates on L vs R should differ so the channels don't freeze in sync.","Preset pack/promo in the source is omitted."],
 [("Insert the buffer delay. Learn the basics: position = delay time, feedback = repeats, segment = how much of the captured audio plays back, reverse toggle.","basics","Sounds like a delay at first"),
  ("Freeze/hold: play a phrase and engage hold. Now position scans through the frozen buffer and segment sets the loop length. Add random start position (and/or an LFO), and use short mode for fine, small segments.","freeze","Micro-loops scanned from the captured buffer"),
  ("Pitch: set +12 st (or a fifth). Each feedback pass pitches up again, so engage the high-cut to tame the cascading brightness. Try sample-rate steps (e.g. 10k, down an octave and again) for temporary pitch effects and crunch; add a little vibrato. Low and high cut together give band-pass tones.","pitch/sr","Rising cascades and crunchy temporary drops"),
  ("Unlink L/R channels so each has its own position, segment, pitch and LFO. Set L +12 st and R −12 st, and set the feedback routing to cross (each side feeds the other).","stereo","Wide image; octaves interleave across channels"),
  ("Map the important controls to macros. Add two LFOs in binary (random on/off) mode at different rates on freeze L and freeze R, set as remote control so they aren't hand-moved.","random freeze","Each channel freezes at random intervals"),
  ("Add two more binary LFOs on reverse L and reverse R, and one random (not binary) LFO with full range on the sample-rate/bandwidth control that steps between octave settings.","random reverse/sr","Random direction flips and octave jumps"),
  ("Optionally add a hybrid reverb, and lower dry/wet so the effect becomes a whisper in the background.","finish","Evocative glitch texture under the dry part")],
 ["With hold on, changing position scans through the same captured audio.","Pitch +12 with feedback produces audibly rising repeats.","L and R freeze/reverse at different times when the binary LFOs run.","Stepping sample rate causes momentary pitch dips."],
 ["micro-loop","buffer","freeze","glitch","pitch-shift","stereo","random-lfo","web-audio"],
 note="Stock-device deep dive; route.py said COVERED but hand-check found per-channel binary freeze/reverse and cross-feedback not covered. Gumroad promo dropped.")
